# XCU continue
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The special built-in utilities are described inside
# utilities/V3_chap02.html (the page utilities/continue.html only
# redirects there), so anchors name V3_chap02.html and the .cov file
# accounts for the units by hand.

assertion  XCU.continue.001
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/return to the top
class      required
says       Without an operand, continue skips the rest of the body of the
           innermost for, while or until loop and starts the next iteration.
test       t/001-innermost.sh

assertion  XCU.continue.002
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/return to the top
class      required
says       continue n returns to the top of the nth enclosing loop,
           abandoning the inner loops; continue 1 is the same as continue.
test       t/002-nth-loop.sh

assertion  XCU.continue.003
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/outermost
class      required
says       When n is greater than the number of enclosing loops, continue
           applies to the outermost enclosing loop.
test       t/003-too-large.sh

assertion  XCU.continue.004
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/repeating the condition list
class      required
says       continue in a while or until loop repeats the condition list; in
           a for loop it takes the next item.
test       t/004-condition-repeated.sh

assertion  XCU.continue.005
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#EXIT STATUS/not an unsigned decimal integer
class      required
says       A continue whose operand is not a positive decimal integer
           returns a non-zero status (or the shell exits with a non-zero
           status).
test       t/005-bad-operand.sh
